{"type":"reasoning","timestamp":1790679997588,"sessionID":"ses_f132db44effejOC7YW0uFAg7SL","part":{"id":"prt_0ecd84d47001QhQgUM9gzBhGPP","messageID":"msg_0ecd83d5400111ivEERufj03kF","sessionID":"ses_f132db44effejOC7YW0uFAg7SL","type":"reasoning","text":"Hmm, this is getting complicated. The threading approach is racy. Let me simplify: the AutoAscend agent calls `env.step(action)` synchronously, and the adapter blocks waiting for the next observation. In my SyncEnv, the agent thread will block inside `step()` until I set `_pending`. So actually I can do it in a single thread if I use a coroutine trick... no.\n\nSimpler approach: make the agent step in the same thread using a generator. Actually AutoAscend's `step` is fully synchronous, calling `env.step`. I can implement `env.step` as: record the action, then... it needs the next observation which requires the outer loop to call env.step(action) on the real env. That's inherently a coroutine.\n\nBut actually — I can just run the real NLE env directly! The agent's `env.step(action)` just needs to return the next observation. I can make a small adapter that drives the real env synchronously:\n\n```python\nclass DirectEnv:\n    def __init__(self, env): self.env = env\n    def step(self, action):\n        obs, r, term, trunc, info = self.env.step(action)\n        return obs, r, term, {}\n```\n\nThat's it! The agent runs in the main thread and the NLE env steps directly. No threading needed. The only difference from the arena is that the arena sandbox runs the bot in a subprocess with an action timeout. But for diagnostics, this is perfect and much simpler.\n\nLet me rewrite.","time":{"start":1790679993672,"end":1790679997582}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1790680002419,"sessionID":"ses_f132db44effejOC7YW0uFAg7SL","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"write","callID":"call_function_3y8z4y08a3km_1","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"\"\"\"In-process diagnostic driver: runs the arena bot directly against NLE.\"\"\"\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport contextlib\nimport json\nimport os\nimport sys\nimport tempfile\nimport time\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\ncache = Path(tempfile.gettempdir()) / \"nethack_arena_submission_cache\"\ncache.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\nos.environ.setdefault(\"XDG_CACHE_HOME\", str(cache / \"xdg\"))\nos.environ.setdefault(\"NUMBA_CACHE_DIR\", str(cache / \"numba\"))\n\nimport warnings\nwarnings.filterwarnings(\"ignore\", category=RuntimeWarning)\n\nsys.path.insert(0, \"/workspace\")\n\nfrom nethackers.arena.environment import NLEEnvironment  # noqa: E402\nfrom nethackers.arena.seeds import trajectory_spec  # noqa: E402\n\nfrom autoascend import agent as autoascend_agent  # noqa: E402\n\n\nclass DirectEnv:\n    def __init__(self, env):\n        self.env = env\n\n    def step(self, action):\n        obs, r, term, trunc, info = self.env.step(action)\n        return obs, r, term, {}\n\n    def debug_tiles(self, *a, **k):\n        return contextlib.nullcontext()\n\n    def debug_log(self, *a, **k):\n        return contextlib.nullcontext()\n\n\ndef main():\n    seed = int(sys.argv[1]) if len(sys.argv) > 1 else 0\n    out = sys.argv[2] if len(sys.argv) > 2 else None\n    budget = float(sys.argv[3]) if len(sys.argv) > 3 else 1200.0\n    spec = trajectory_spec(\"public\", \"local\", seed)\n    env = NLEEnvironment(1_000_000, 10_000, \"wiz-hum-cha-mal\")\n    obs = env.reset(spec)\n    direct = DirectEnv(env)\n\n    holder = {}\n\n    class Holder:\n        pass\n\n    from autoascend.agent import Agent\n    ag = Agent(direct, panic_on_errors=False)\n\n    # wrap step to trace\n    orig_step = ag.step\n    trace = []\n    last = [0, 0]\n    state = {\"t0\": time.time()}\n\n    def step(action, *a, **k):\n        r = orig_step(action, *a, **k)\n        o = ag.last_observation\n        if o is not None:\n            bl = o[\"blstats\"]\n            key = (int(bl[18]), int(bl[12]), int(bl[11]))\n            if key != last[0]:\n                trace.append({\"turn\": int(bl[0]), \"xp\": key[0], \"depth\": key[1], \"hp\": key[2]})\n                last[0] = key\n        if time.time() - state[\"t0\"] > budget:\n            raise RuntimeError(\"budget\")\n        return r\n\n    ag.step = step\n\n    err = None\n    try:\n        ag.main()\n    except autoascend_agent.AgentFinished:\n        pass\n    except RuntimeError as e:\n        err = str(e)\n    except BaseException:\n        import traceback\n        err = traceback.format_exc(limit=20)\n\n    m = env.metrics()\n    info = {\n        \"seed\": seed, \"turns\": m.turns, \"progress\": m.progress,\n        \"death\": m.cause_of_death, \"end_status\": m.end_status,\n        \"err\": err,\n        \"panics\": [str(p) for p in ag.all_panics[-12:]],\n    }\n    if out:\n        Path(out).write_text(json.dumps({\"info\": info, \"trace\": trace}, indent=1))\n    print(json.dumps(info, indent=1))\n    env.close()\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n","filePath":"/home/agent/nhwork/diag.py"},"output":"Wrote file successfully.","metadata":{"diagnostics":{},"filepath":"/home/agent/nhwork/diag.py","exists":true,"truncated":false},"title":"home/agent/nhwork/diag.py","time":{"start":1790680002397,"end":1790680002417}},"id":"prt_0ecd85c91001nngo1Uxq78g7UA","sessionID":"ses_f132db44effejOC7YW0uFAg7SL","messageID":"msg_0ecd83d5400111ivEERufj03kF"}}
