{"type":"reasoning","timestamp":1790680106967,"sessionID":"ses_f132db44effejOC7YW0uFAg7SL","part":{"id":"prt_0ecd9f086001jyPkMEfS6hOhmJ","messageID":"msg_0ecd9e98d001iT60RSEAsg8nYc","sessionID":"ses_f132db44effejOC7YW0uFAg7SL","type":"reasoning","text":"Interesting — the trace ordering is odd (turn resets?). Because the `trace` recorded `turn` as blstats[0] which is time... hmm the values 6, 47, 7, 44, 12, 40, 46, 45 look scrambled. That's because DirectEnv.step is called during recursive agent steps, and `ag.last_observation` may lag. Whatever.\n\nKey data: XP goes 1→2→3→4→5→6, HP grows 12→18→25→34→41→50. So the wizard levels from 12 HP to 50 HP by XP 6. Then at turn ~13,697 she dies to a goblin at HP... let's see the final. The trace's last entry is xp 6, hp 46 — so she died at HP ≤46? Hmm, max HP at XL6 would be ~50. So she died at around 46/50 HP? Hmm, that doesn't sound like a low-HP death. Wait no — the trace entries are recorded mid-recursion so they're not reliable in order.\n\nLet me improve the tracing: record at the point where the agent's `update()` completes (i.e., a full turn). Simpler: record in DirectEnv.step only when the action is a *movement/direction* action... Still messy.\n\nActually better: use `ag.update` hook. Or simplest: track by reading the last blstats at the *end* (in _run after main). But I want the history.\n\nAlternative: record only when `int(bl[0])` (turn) increases monotonically, i.e. record when turn changes. Let me record on turn change: store {turn, xp, depth, hp}.\n\nLet me restructure: keep dict keyed by turn.\n\nAlso I want to log key events: messages like \"You kill the goblin!\", level up, spell casting, item pickups, and the agent's strategy decisions.\n\nLet me write a better diagnostic that:\n1. Records XP/HP/turn timeline.\n2. Records the death context (last 60 messages).\n3. Records the agent's stats (stats_logger).\n\nLet me look at stats_logger to see what's available.","time":{"start":1790680100998,"end":1790680106963}}}
