{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1790680147417,"sessionID":"ses_f132db44effejOC7YW0uFAg7SL","part":{"id":"prt_0ecdaa5d4001rrUkM9DW3N9PIi","messageID":"msg_0ecda9eee001KxkwzbnSa37611","sessionID":"ses_f132db44effejOC7YW0uFAg7SL","type":"step-start"}}
{"type":"reasoning","timestamp":1790680158364,"sessionID":"ses_f132db44effejOC7YW0uFAg7SL","part":{"id":"prt_0ecdaa5d6001T1uhBGbEwRwrmT","messageID":"msg_0ecda9eee001KxkwzbnSa37611","sessionID":"ses_f132db44effejOC7YW0uFAg7SL","type":"reasoning","text":"**190 kills** in 13,697 turns and it only reached XP 6! That's 72 turns per kill. That's terribly inefficient. And the XP required for XL 1→7 is 20+40+80+160+320+640 = 1260 XP. 190 kills ≈ 190 XP... hmm, more than 190. Anyway.\n\nWait, XP 6 at 190 kills. Human XP table: L2:20, L3:40, L4:80, L5:160, L6:320, L7:640. Total to L7 = 1260. 190 kills can't give 1260 XP unless kills give ~6 XP each. Hmm, in NetHack each monster kill gives 1 XP base plus bonus for \"hard\" kills? Actually monsters have an `mlet` and XP is 1 per kill, plus... hmm. Actually in NetHack, killing a monster gives experience points equal to 1 (times multiplier). Hmm, but there are bonus points for e.g. killing with certain weapons.\n\nHmm, wait. Let me reconsider: maybe blstats[18] is not XP level. Let me check NLE_BL indices. In progress.py, BL_XP = 18, and it's used as \"Xp:{int(blstats[18])}\" with Xp:1 = 0.0. So index 18 is experience level. OK.\n\nSo 190 kills → XL 6? That means ~6.6 XP per kill on average. Hmm, in NetHack, each kill gives 1 XP... Actually no! In NetHack, `u.uevent.xp` ... let me recall `xlev_gain()` in levregion.c? No — XP is gained in `mon_died`/`mnexpand`? Actually:\n\n```c\nvoid\nmon_give_experience(...)\n```\nHmm. In NetHack 3.6, `u.ucred`? No. Let me recall: in `mon.c`, `mon_kill()`... Actually the relevant is in `nhlua`? Hmm.\n\nIn NetHack 3.6, XP is granted in `upstairs`? No. It's in `mon.c: mon_died()`? Hmm, actually I remember: `void gain_experience(int n)` in levregion.c? Let me not guess.\n\nActually the key: In NetHack 3.6, killing a monster gives experience equal to its \"experience points\", and monster experience is 1 for most, but there's `mdef->mlet` based XP in `monst.c` `msexperience`? Hmm. Actually I recall in `mon.c`:\n\n```c\n/*mon.c*/\nvoid\nmon_give_experience(mtmp, killed_by_you)\n```\nHmm.\n\nOK regardless, empirically 190 kills → XL 6, and 13,697 turns. 72 turns/kill is the striking number. The bot is spending most of its time doing something other than killing.\n\nAlso: **122 panics** in 13,697 turns. Panics are expensive (each panic = ESC ESC + full state update + re-plan).\n\nAnd 4,053 messages in 13,697 turns.\n\nNow the crucial question: what is the wizard doing all that time? Let's look at the message log and the strategy usage.\n\nKey hypothesis forming: **The wizard has spells and never uses them.** Let me check the inventory at start. Let me add a dump of the initial inventory and known spells.\n\nLet me also count the actions by type. Let me instrument the message log for key phrases.\n\nLet me look at the last messages and a sample.","time":{"start":1790680147414,"end":1790680158359}}}
