{"type":"reasoning","timestamp":1790680262948,"sessionID":"ses_f132db44effejOC7YW0uFAg7SL","part":{"id":"prt_0ecdc37d5001pSiFl137at3wu3","messageID":"msg_0ecdc285a001u80pN1L30tkNcj","sessionID":"ses_f132db44effejOC7YW0uFAg7SL","type":"reasoning","text":"HUGE finding. Look at the end of the game:\n\n```\n{'turn': 12441, 'xp': 6, ..., 'exp_pts': 598, 'maxhp': 50}\n{'turn': 12845, 'xp': 5, ..., 'exp_pts': 319, 'maxhp': 41, 'hunger_state': 4}\n```\n\n**Experience points went from 598 DOWN to 319 and the XP level from 6 DOWN to 5!** The wizard got **polymorphed** into a monster! Max HP dropped 50 → 41, hunger_state jumped to 4 (fainting).\n\nAt turn ~12,800 the wizard was **polymorphed**. That's why: \"You faint from lack of food\", \"You swap places with your large cat\", \"Are you sure you want to pray? You begin praying to Anhur. You finish your prayer. You feel that Anhur is displeased.\"\n\nWait, actually looking at the last messages: \"You swap places with your large cat\" — that's the polymorph into a feline! And \"The large cat is confused from hunger.\"\n\nSo around turn 12,800 the wizard polymorphed into a cat. From then to death (13,697) she wanders as a cat and dies to a goblin.\n\nHmm, wait. Also AC is 8-9 the whole game! A wizard with AC 9? That's from a robe? Wizards start with... hmm, AC 9 at turn 1 with 12 HP. Human wizard starts with a \"cloak\"? Hmm, in NetHack the wizard's initial equipment depends on alignment: for chaotic, `init_items`... Actually wizards get a \"dagger\" or nothing. AC 9 means basically naked. Yeah: AC 9 = no armor.\n\nWait, blstats[16] is armor_class. AC 9 = naked. Right.\n\nOK. And XP: 598 exp points at turn 12,441 but only 190 kills. So ~3 XP per kill. Human XP thresholds: L2: 20, L3: 40, L4: 80, L5: 160, L6: 320, L7: 640. Cumulative to L6 = 300. Yes matches (598 > 320 → XP 6). To reach L7 needs 640. So at 598 points at turn 12,441, she was ~40 XP short of L7!\n\nAnd the rate of XP accumulation: from turn 8027 (343 pts) to 12441 (598 pts) = 255 points in 4414 turns = 17.3 turns/point. And each point is ~3 XP per kill → ~52 turns per kill. 190 kills in 13,697 turns = 72 turns/kill.\n\nSo: **the bot is extremely inefficient at finding/killing monsters.** It spends 72 turns per kill. Most of those turns are SEARCH (2050) and SPACE (1614) and NUM_5 (1430 — hmm, that's a digit; likely from `#te` terrain? no... \"NUM_5\" is from search(max_count) typing \"5\"? Actually `search()` with max_count>1 types str(max_count). Hmm, or from \"5\" typed in some menu).\n\nHmm, so the fundamental problem: the bot spends its time searching/exploring rather than fighting. And the wizard's melee is weak, so fights are long and risky.\n\n**The key insight for scoring**: progression = XP level. The bot must level up. It's an XP-farming bot that farms too slowly and dies.\n\nNow what's the single change with the highest leverage?\n\nOptions:\n1. **Cast spells.** A wizard with fireball/magic missile kills much faster. XP per turn goes way up. AND safer (ranged). The game rules file hints at this strongly. Does the wizard have a spellbook? Let me check the inventory.\n\n2. **Polymorph handling** — a one-off, seeds-specific. Not the main lever.\n\n3. **Efficiency of exploration** — e.g., use \"detect monsters\" or the `search` behavior.\n\nLet me check the starting inventory to see if spells are available. This is decisive.\n\nLet me dump the inventory at the beginning of a game.","time":{"start":1790680250325,"end":1790680262940}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1790680285974,"sessionID":"ses_f132db44effejOC7YW0uFAg7SL","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"call_function_eu3t29ig46p7_1","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /workspace && timeout 300 python - <<'EOF' 2>&1 | tail -40\nimport os, sys, tempfile, warnings, threading, contextlib, json\nfrom pathlib import Path\ncache = Path(tempfile.gettempdir()) / \"nethack_arena_submission_cache\"\nos.environ.setdefault(\"XDG_CACHE_HOME\", str(cache / \"xdg\")); os.environ.setdefault(\"NUMBA_CACHE_DIR\", str(cache / \"numba\"))\nwarnings.filterwarnings(\"ignore\", category=RuntimeWarning)\nsys.path.insert(0, \"/workspace\"); sys.setrecursionlimit(200000)\nfrom nethackers.arena.environment import NLEEnvironment\nfrom nethackers.arena.seeds import trajectory_spec\nfrom autoascend import agent as A\nfrom nle.nethack import ACTIONS\n\ndef run():\n    env = NLEEnvironment(1_000_000, 10_000, \"wiz-hum-cha-mal\")\n    obs = env.reset(trajectory_spec(\"public\",\"local\",0))\n    class D:\n        n = 0\n        def step(self, action):\n            res = env.step(ACTIONS.index(action)); D.n += 1\n            return res[0], res[1], res[2], {}\n        def debug_tiles(self,*a,**k): return contextlib.nullcontext()\n        def debug_log(self,*a,**k): return contextlib.nullcontext()\n    ag = A.Agent(D(), panic_on_errors=True)\n    d = D()\n    ag._d = d\n    # step a few times to let parse() run, then dump\n    orig = ag.step\n    def step(action, *a, **k):\n        r = orig(action, *a, **k)\n        if d.n == 12:\n            print(\"=== after\", d.n, \"steps\")\n            print(\"char:\", ag.character.role, ag.character.race, ag.character.alignment)\n            print(\"known_spells:\", getattr(ag.character, \"known_spells\", None))\n            print(\"skill:\", getattr(ag.character, \"skill\", None))\n            for it in ag.inventory.items:\n                print(\"  inv:\", it, \"|\", getattr(it,'category',None))\n            print(\"messages:\", ag.message)\n            print(\"---raw tty---\")\n            for line in obs.get(\"tty_chars\", [])[:24]:\n                print(bytes(line).decode().replace(\"\\0\",\" \"))\n        return r\n    ag.step = step\n    try:\n        ag.main()\n    except BaseException as e:\n        pass\nthreading.stack_size(512*1024*1024)\nt = threading.Thread(target=run); t.start(); t.join()\nEOF","timeout":320000},"output":"    |.......|                                                                   \n    |.......|                                                                   \n    |.......|                                                                   \n    ---------                                                                   \n                                                                                \n                                                                                \n                                                                                \n                                                                                \nAgent the Evoker               St:12 Dx:14 Co:12 In:18 Wi:8 Ch:11 Chaotic S:0   \nDlvl:1 $:0 HP:12(12) Pw:6(6) AC:9 Xp:1/0 T:1                                    \n=== after 12 steps\nchar: 12 0 0\nknown_spells: None\nskill: None\nmessages: \n---raw tty---\n                                                                                \n                                                                                \n                                                                                \n                                                                                \n                                                                                \n                                                                                \n                                                                                \n                                                                            