{"type":"reasoning","timestamp":1790680298799,"sessionID":"ses_f132db44effejOC7YW0uFAg7SL","part":{"id":"prt_0ecdcd03a001QVIWGbzABrBs06","messageID":"msg_0ecdcc310001bmDDuBOEbpnquE","sessionID":"ses_f132db44effejOC7YW0uFAg7SL","type":"reasoning","text":"HP:12(12) AC:9, no equipment. The character is \"Agent the Evoker\" (role Evoker = Wizard). Wait — \"Agent\" is the NLE character name override.\n\n**No starting weapon, no armor, no spellbook.** In NetHack 3.6, the Wizard's starting equipment is: for a \"not demigod\" wizard, `Role uwizard` init gives... let me recall role.c:\n\n```c\n    case Wizard:\n\tif (Role uwizard) { ... }\n```\n\nHmm. In NetHack 3.6 role.c `init_role`:\n```c\n    case Wizard:\n\tif (!rn2(4)) { ... }\n```\nHmm. Actually the standard wizard start: \"You are skilled in spellcasting\" ... In `u_init.c` for Wizard: \n```c\n\tcase Wizard:\n\t    /* no innate equipment */\n\t    break;\n```\nHmm — actually I recall in NetHack 3.6, a Wizard starts with a cloak? No. Let me check: the Wizard's inventory at start: \"You are carrying: nothing\" — actually for Wizard you get 1-2 spells? Hmm no. In NetHack 3.6, the **apprentice** gets... Hmm.\n\nActually I'm fairly sure the Wizard in NetHack 3.6 starts with **no equipment** and must find a spellbook. Wait, no. Let me recall the \"welcome\" message: for Wizard \"You have arcane knowledge...\" Hmm.\n\nThe screen dump shows HP:12(12) AC:9 and Xp:1/0, and the message list is empty. And `ag.inventory.items` printed nothing. So the wizard starts naked with no spells. Confirmed.\n\nHmm, but wait — pw:6(6) = 6 pw. Casting requires energy. OK.\n\nSo: **the wizard has NO spellbook and NO known spells at the start.** Spells require finding a spellbook, reading it, and knowing the spell. That's a big ask. Though — hmm, wait. Actually, in NetHack 3.6 the Wizard DOES start with a spellbook! Let me check: `role.c`:\n\n```c\n    case Wizard:\n\tif (Role uwizard) {\n\t    /* should be the case for any chaos wizard */\n\t}\n```\n\nHmm. Let me just test in-game: I'll type `#\\i` or check `dumplog`. Actually easier: the inv_strs from the observation.\n\nHmm, but the printed `ag.inventory.items` was empty. Let me double check by printing inv_strs from the observation.\n\nActually — I recall now! In NetHack 3.6, `init_role()` for Wizard: nothing, BUT `u_init.c` has:\n```c\n    case Wizard:\n\t...\n```\nHmm. Actually the answer: In NetHack, wizards start with a **spellbook containing 1 random spell** — no wait, that's the *Apprentice*? No, the Apprentice (role \"Apprentice\" in wizard variant) starts with 1-3 spells.\n\nHmm, let me just check: the message when the game starts for a wizard. Let me look at the initial tty message. It was empty. Let's grep inv_strs.\n\nLet me test directly.","time":{"start":1790680289338,"end":1790680298793}}}
