{"type":"reasoning","timestamp":1790680409463,"sessionID":"ses_f132db44effejOC7YW0uFAg7SL","part":{"id":"prt_0ecde5fd0001rFdB23nnlmDj0W","messageID":"msg_0ecde57410017Ua70Sr5MLj1IM","sessionID":"ses_f132db44effejOC7YW0uFAg7SL","type":"reasoning","text":"Massive findings:\n\n**Seed 13: the wizard is CONSTANTLY fainting from lack of food (hunger_state 3-4 = WEAK/FAINTING) for thousands of turns.** She has a housecat pet that keeps eating the corpses! \"The housecat eats a jackal corpse.\" \"The housecat picks up a lichen corpse. You kill the brown mold!... The housecat drops a lichen corpse. The housecat picks up a lichen corpse.\" — the pet is *stealing the food*.\n\nAlso she's attacking brown mold (stationary, COLD damage) pointlessly.\n\n**Seed 3:** She wrote \"Elbereth\" in the dust, then kept walking into a **grid bug** and got zapped to death. Note \"You faint from lack of food\" again, and the grid bug killed her while she was at low energy.\n\nHmm, actually the elbereth engraving: `elbereth_action` fires when HP < 30. She engraved Elbereth and then... the fight2 `wait_action` would keep her there. But she moved away.\n\nOK. Let me now consider the big picture again.\n\n**The single biggest structural finding: the score is XP, the bot farms XP slowly, and the bot is a mess in the early game.**\n\nLet me now consider what change is (a) one focused idea, (b) plausible to help most seeds, (c) doesn't tune to seeds.\n\nLet me re-examine: **Why does the bot kill so slowly?** 72 turns/kill. Let me look at the exploration logic to understand the loop. Let me check `exploration_logic.py` — especially how it decides to search vs. move.\n\nActually, hold on. Let me reconsider one specific, high-leverage, well-grounded idea:\n\n### Idea A: Cast the starting spellbook (learn + cast force bolt), and zap the wand of magic missile.\n\nEvidence: the bot NEVER casts (0 cast events in 15,000 steps), never reads a spellbook, and has a blessed spellbook of force bolt + wand of magic missile sitting in its pack. For a Wizard, this is the single largest untapped source of damage. force bolt at XL6 = 1d6+6 per bolt × up to 3 bolts. The quarterstaff +1 melee at level 0 does ~1-3 damage a hit. So a single force bolt ≈ several melee rounds.\n\nBut: energy. Wizard starts with 6 energy. Energy regen is 1 per ~3-5 turns early. So casting is very limited early. Still, force bolt + magic missile wand is strictly better than the quarterstaff, and it also works at range (safer).\n\nRisk: implementing spell casting requires parsing the known-spells view (`Z` command → \"Cast which spell?\"). There's already `parse_spellcast_view` in character.py! And `agent.cast(spell_name, direction)`. It's mostly written but disabled. Let me look at it.\n\nHmm, but the comment says \"TODO: parse for other spellcaster classes\" — it only handles... let me read character.py.\n\n### Idea B: Fix the food problem.\nPet eats corpses; wizard starves. Also corpses rot. 44 faints.\n\n### Idea C: Speed up the kill loop.\n\nLet me look at character.py parse_spellcast_view and parse_enhance_view to judge feasibility of Idea A.\n\nActually, let me reconsider the scale of the prize. The bot needs to double/triple its XP rate to change the XP ladder position. With ~13,000-32,000 turns available, going from Xp:6 to Xp:8 requires 4× the XP. That's a huge ask for any change.\n\nHmm. So maybe the more reliable lever is: **survive longer**. Look at the distribution again:\n- 3 seeds die at 3,000-5,200 turns (Xp 3-4).\n- 4 seeds die at 11,900-17,700 (Xp 6-7).\n- 8 seeds die at 20,700-32,300 (Xp 8-10).\n\nThe step from Xp:6 (0.0369) to Xp:7 (0.0508) to Xp:8 (0.0745) is what the long-lived seeds get. If a change made seeds 0, 1, 6, 12 (Xp 6, dying at 12-17k turns) survive to 25k+ turns they'd reach Xp 8 (+0.038 each = +0.010 mean). And seeds 3, 10, 13 from Xp 3-4 to Xp 6+ (+0.015 each).\n\nAlternatively if a change makes the bot kill 2x faster, seeds would level about 2x faster in wall-clock turns, which given the same survival time means ~+1 XP level. That's similar magnitude but requires fewer mistakes.\n\nHmm. Honestly, both point to the same thing: **make the wizard fight better and live longer**.\n\nLet me look for the single most *specific* and *defensible* mechanism.\n\nLet me dig into what actually causes death. Let me get the death context for the mid-range seeds (0, 1, 6, 12) to see if there's a common, fixable cause.\n\nActually, I already know seed 0's death: fainting from hunger + goblin. Let's check 1, 6, 12, 5, 2, 14, 8, 7, 9, 11, 4 quickly. Let me run diag on all seeds in background and analyze. Each takes ~20-50s. 15 seeds ≈ 10 min sequentially, or ~4 min with 4 parallel on 1 CPU... actually 1 CPU, so sequential is the same. Let me just run them all sequentially in the background and think meanwhile.\n\nLet me kick that off.","time":{"start":1790680391632,"end":1790680409456}}}
