{"type":"reasoning","timestamp":1790680580794,"sessionID":"ses_f132db44effejOC7YW0uFAg7SL","part":{"id":"prt_0ece128e7001F1fQXWYIUEvSfi","messageID":"msg_0ece1204e001dbrW7w3uD61w2H","sessionID":"ses_f132db44effejOC7YW0uFAg7SL","type":"reasoning","text":"The read attempt didn't work. Inventory letters: with 14 items and a `-` letter in class... let me figure out the letters. The inv_strs show items a..n plus a blank (wielded item '-'). Actually in NetHack the letter class for weapons is '-', armor is '[' , etc. Order of letters in inventory display: class 0 (misc) = a,b,c..., then class 1 (amulet) = '\"', class 2 (armor) = '[', class 3 (ring) = '=', class 4 (scroll) = '?', class 5 (spellbook) = '?', hmm.\n\nActually the class letters: \n- ILLCOL: 0 = 'a'-'c' etc (misc), 1 = '\"' (amulet), 2 = '[' (armor), 3 = '=' (ring), 4 = '?' (scroll), 5 = '`' (spellbook), 6 = '(' (potions), 7 = '!' (tools), 8 = ')' (wands), 9 = '[' (weapons), 10 = '=' (armor), ...\n\nHmm, NetHack's inventory class letters in `invent.c`:\n```c\nchar ilc_classes[] = {\n    '-', '=', '?', '!', '/', '(', ')', '[', '{', '}', '\\\\'  ???\n```\nHmm. Let me recall the actual:\n```c\nconst char ilc_classes[] = {\n    /* 0 */ '-', /* weapons */\n    /* 1 */ '=', /* armor */\n    /* 2 */ '(', /* rings */\n    /* 3 */ '\"', /* amulets */\n    /* 4 */ '?', /* tools */\n    /* 5 */ '`', /* food */\n    /* 6 */ ';', /* potions */\n    /* 7 */ ':', /* scrolls */\n    /* 8 */ '/', /* spellbooks */\n    /* 9 */ ',', /* wands */\n    /* 10 */ '~', /* gems */\n    ...\n};\n```\nYes! That's right: weapons '-', armor '=', rings '(', amulets '\"', tools '?', food '`', potions ';', scrolls ':', spellbooks '/', wands ',', gems '~', rocks '*', boulders '0'... \n\nSo the spellbook of force bolt is read with `/` and the wand is `,`.\n\nLet me redo: press 'r' then '/' then 'a' (first spellbook).\n\nAlso for the cast view: pressing 'Z' showed nothing. Because the wizard knows no spells, the message would be \"You don't know any spells.\" Hmm, the message was empty. Maybe NLE's message handling. Let's look at the top line... The screen shows nothing at the top. Hmm.\n\nLet me be more careful and print the full screen + message after each step. Let me improve the probe to be step-by-step verbose.\n\nActually, the important question is whether the whole spell pipeline works. Let me instead do this inside the real agent framework: use the agent's own machinery, which handles the message/popup parsing. That's the real test.\n\nLet me write a probe that runs the agent but, at a chosen turn, executes a scripted sequence using agent primitives (atom_operation, type_text, etc.) and prints the popup.\n\nThat's cleaner. Let me do that.","time":{"start":1790680574183,"end":1790680580790}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1790680585163,"sessionID":"ses_f132db44effejOC7YW0uFAg7SL","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"write","callID":"call_function_sk4g4hmd4b9n_1","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"\"\"\"Probe spell machinery through the real Agent primitives.\"\"\"\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport contextlib\nimport json\nimport os\nimport sys\nimport tempfile\nimport threading\nimport time\nimport warnings\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\ncache = Path(tempfile.gettempdir()) / \"nethack_arena_submission_cache\"\ncache.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\nos.environ.setdefault(\"XDG_CACHE_HOME\", str(cache / \"xdg\"))\nos.environ.setdefault(\"NUMBA_CACHE_DIR\", str(cache / \"numba\"))\nwarnings.filterwarnings(\"ignore\", category=RuntimeWarning)\nsys.path.insert(0, \"/workspace\")\n\nfrom nethackers.arena.environment import NLEEnvironment  # noqa: E402\nfrom nethackers.arena.seeds import trajectory_spec  # noqa: E402\nfrom nle.nethack import ACTIONS as _ACTIONS  # noqa: E402\n\n\nclass DirectEnv:\n    def __init__(self, env):\n        self.env = env\n        self.agent = None\n        self.t0 = time.time()\n        self.budget = 1e18\n\n    def step(self, action):\n        res = self.env.step(_ACTIONS.index(action))\n        if time.time() - self.t0 > self.budget:\n            raise RuntimeError(\"budget\")\n        return res[0], res[1], res[2], {}\n\n    def debug_tiles(self, *a, **k):\n        return contextlib.nullcontext()\n\n    def debug_log(self, *a, **k):\n        return contextlib.nullcontext()\n\n\ndef screen(obs, n=24):\n    return \"\\n\".join(\n        bytes(l).decode(errors=\"replace\").replace(\"\\0\", \" \").rstrip()\n        for l in obs[\"tty_chars\"][:n])\n\n\ndef run():\n    seed = int(sys.argv[1]) if len(sys.argv) > 1 else 0\n    env = NLEEnvironment(1_000_000, 10_000, \"wiz-hum-cha-mal\")\n    obs = env.reset(trajectory_spec(\"public\", \"local\", seed))\n    d = DirectEnv(env)\n    from autoascend import agent as A\n    ag = A.Agent(d, panic_on_errors=True)\n    d.agent = ag\n\n    # do the init atom operation only\n    with ag.atom_operation():\n        ag.step(A.Command.ESC)\n        ag.step(A.Command.ESC)\n        ag.character.parse()\n        ag.character.parse_enhance_view()\n    print(\"char:\", ag.character)\n    print(\"inventory letters:\")\n    for it in ag.inventory.items:\n        print(\"   \", ag.inventory.items.get_letter(it), it)\n    print(\"blstats energy\", ag.blstats.energy, \"/\", ag.blstats.max_energy)\n\n    # read the spellbook\n    from nle.nethack import actions as Ac\n    letter = None\n    for it in ag.inventory.items:\n        if getattr(it, \"category\", None) == 10:  # SPBOOK_CLASS\n            letter = ag.inventory.items.get_letter(it)\n            print(\"spellbook\", it, \"letter\", letter)\n    if letter is not None:\n        with ag.atom_operation():\n            ag.step(Ac.Command.READ)\n            ag.step(letter)\n            for _ in range(6):\n                ag.step(\"y\" if \"really\" in ag.message else \" \")\n            print(\"after read msg:\", repr(ag.message))\n            print(\"popup:\", ag.popup)\n\n    # open the cast view\n    with ag.atom_operation():\n        ag.step(Ac.Command.CAST)\n        for _ in range(4):\n            ag.step(\" \")\n    print(\"=== cast view ===\")\n    print(screen(ag.last_observation))\n    print(\"message:\", repr(ag.message))\n    print(\"popup:\", ag.popup)\n    env.close()\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    sys.setrecursionlimit(100000)\n    threading.stack_size(256 * 1024 * 1024)\n    t = threading.Thread(target=run)\n    t.start()\n    t.join()\n","filePath":"/home/agent/nhwork/probe2.py"},"output":"Wrote file successfully.","metadata":{"diagnostics":{},"filepath":"/home/agent/nhwork/probe2.py","exists":false,"truncated":false},"title":"home/agent/nhwork/probe2.py","time":{"start":1790680585153,"end":1790680585161}},"id":"prt_0ece142b8001xI39CKX7WPRlKs","sessionID":"ses_f132db44effejOC7YW0uFAg7SL","messageID":"msg_0ece1204e001dbrW7w3uD61w2H"}}
