{"type":"reasoning","timestamp":1790680604311,"sessionID":"ses_f132db44effejOC7YW0uFAg7SL","part":{"id":"prt_0ece19055001kr7258Old4tyBA","messageID":"msg_0ece1865c001ERHGtZbK9ZwbjI","sessionID":"ses_f132db44effejOC7YW0uFAg7SL","type":"reasoning","text":"Oops — reading the spellbook with 'r' then 'l' — 'l' is the letter... but wait, the \"Blind\" status appeared. The 'r' command: `r` then 'l' then 'y' prompts. Hmm, actually after `ag.step(Ac.Command.READ)` and `ag.step(letter)`, the prompt \"Read what?\" — but we need to check: maybe 'l' wasn't accepted as the letter. Then my loop typed ' ' which triggered... hmm, \"Blind\" appeared — that's from the blindfold 'n'? No.\n\nHmm, \"Blind\" in the status line. Something went wrong — probably typing spaces answered a y/n prompt and then subsequent keys did something weird.\n\nLet me be more careful and check the message at each step. Let me modify: after each step print the message.\n\nActually, a subtlety: `ag.step()` for text input goes through `update()` which handles `misc[1]` (entering text) etc. Hmm, `update()` checks `observation['misc'][1]` → \"entering text\" → steps ESC. That would cancel our typing! Let me check: `misc[1]` is `nle`'s \"entering text\" flag... In agent.update:\n```\nif observation['misc'][1]:  # entering text\n    ... step ESC\n```\nSo if the game is in a text-entry mode, the agent sends ESC. That could be interfering.\n\nLet me print message at each step.","time":{"start":1790680600661,"end":1790680604307}}}
