{"type":"reasoning","timestamp":1790680827991,"sessionID":"ses_f132db44effejOC7YW0uFAg7SL","part":{"id":"prt_0ece4c7b40011okyaCZrXApFvR","messageID":"msg_0ece4bf45001wj7ZZ16hai0WaX","sessionID":"ses_f132db44effejOC7YW0uFAg7SL","type":"reasoning","text":"Casting works: \"The spell hits the kobold! You kill the kobold!\" and \"The spell hits the newt! You kill the newt!\".\n\nBut: **\"You don't have enough energy to cast that spell.\" 193 times!** — the energy check is broken. The wizard has 6 energy and my `spell_energy_cost('force bolt')` = 2*1+1 = 3, so `can_cast` returns True with energy 6, yet the game says not enough energy.\n\nHmm, \"You don't have enough energy to cast that spell.\" — In NetHack, you need energy >= the spell cost AND... hmm. Actually the message is `You don't have enough energy to cast that spell.` when `u.uen < energycost(spell)`. Hmm, 6 energy should be plenty for force bolt.\n\nOh! Wait. The problem: `self.blstats.energy` is index 14. Let me double check whether index 14 is really `energy`. The BLStats namedtuple: index 0=x,1=y,2=strength_percentage,3=strength,4=dexterity,5=constitution,6=intelligence,7=wisdom,8=charisma,9=score,10=hitpoints,11=max_hitpoints,12=depth,13=gold,14=energy,15=max_energy,16=armor_class,17=monster_level,18=experience_level,19=experience_points,20=time,21=hunger_state.\n\nEarlier, my snapshot printed hp=bl[10], maxhp=bl[11] and it matched the tty (12(12) at start). And energy bl[14] gave 6 at start which matched Pw:6(6). So index 14 IS energy.\n\nSo energy is 6, cost is... hmm. Wait — the message \"You don't have enough energy to cast that spell.\" Hmm, in NetHack the *cast* itself is fine but the wizard needs `u.uen >= energycost`. energycost for a level-1 spell... \n\nHmm, hold on! Actually maybe the issue is different: the message could come from a *different* spell. `best_attack_spell` picks from `spell_fail_chance` for names in ATTACK_SPELL_DAMAGE. Only 'force bolt' qualifies (haste self is escape). So it casts force bolt.\n\nHmm, but \"You don't have enough energy to cast that spell.\" 193 times. And 193 \"Unknown command ' '.\" — the cast flow is sending a stray space.\n\nHmm! Energy might be dropping to 0 as we cast repeatedly, and the wizard is stuck in a loop trying to cast with 0 energy. Because `can_cast` uses `blstats.energy` which... should be 0 then. Unless `blstats` is stale.\n\nAH — I see the bug. `best_attack_spell` is called from `cast_priority` during `get_available_actions`. But the check happens once per decision; the agent picks the action, casts (spending energy), and then... hmm.\n\nWait, actually let me reconsider: energy regen is very slow. Force bolt costs some energy. After a few casts energy hits 0, and the message repeats. And \"Unknown command ' '\" 193 times suggests the `cast()` helper is sending spaces because 'In what direction?' never appears (because the game rejects the cast before asking for a direction).\n\nSo: when the cast fails for lack of energy, `agent.cast` still types the letter and then 3 spaces → \"Unknown command ' '\". That's the source of the stray spaces.\n\nFix: the priority should be gated on actually having energy, and `cast` should not spam. But the real question is why `can_cast` returns True at 0 energy.\n\nLet me print the energy. Possibly `blstats.energy` isn't refreshed... Actually `self.blstats` is set in `update()`. During `fight2`, `get_priorities` is called after an update. Should be fresh.\n\nHmm — unless force bolt's energy cost is > 6. Let me look at NetHack 3.6's `energycost`:\n\n```c\nint\nenergycost(int spell)\n{\n    int energy;\n\n    energy = 3 * (spell_lev(spell) + 1) / 2; /* level 1 costs 3, level 2 costs 4, ... */\n    ...\n}\n```\nHmm that's 3 for force bolt, and we have 6.\n\nHmm, wait. Actually in NetHack 3.6, casting also requires `u.uen >= (spell_lev(spell) + 1)`? Hmm.\n\nLet me just measure. Let me add a debug print... Actually, better: let me look at what happens. 193 attempts. Let me look at the timeline of the messages to see the first occurrence and what the energy was.\n\nActually, let me reconsider: maybe `blstats.energy` (index 14) is NOT energy. Let me verify against the tty: I printed `energy: bl[14]` = 6 at turn 1 and the tty showed \"Pw:6(6)\". That's a strong match. Hmm, but at turn 403 (xp 2) energy showed 20 and turn 1605 (xp 3) showed 26... max energy at xp2 should be 20 (10*(1+1)) — hmm, so bl[14] was at max. Hmm, that's suspicious: energy exactly = max for most snapshots. If bl[14] were, e.g., \"energy\" it'd fluctuate. Unless regen is fast at higher levels and the snapshot is at max.\n\nHmm. Let me just directly test: print bl[14] and the tty Pw line together during a cast.\n\nActually, simpler: let me look at NLE's blstats definition to get the exact index mapping.\n\nLet me search the NLE headers.","time":{"start":1790680811444,"end":1790680827984}}}
