{"type":"reasoning","timestamp":1790680869627,"sessionID":"ses_f132db44effejOC7YW0uFAg7SL","part":{"id":"prt_0ece59c19001kl8Kg0WzyjxMG1","messageID":"msg_0ece595f5001R0v43rV5DvGAHj","sessionID":"ses_f132db44effejOC7YW0uFAg7SL","type":"reasoning","text":"Let me continue. So index 14 IS energy. So why \"You don't have enough energy to cast that spell.\" with energy 6?\n\nHmm, wait. Let me reconsider. In NetHack 3.6, there's a message \"You don't have enough energy to cast that spell.\" which is `pline(\"You don't have enough energy to cast that spell.\")` in `do_cast` when `u.uen < energycost(spell)`. \n\nenergycost in NetHack 3.6 (`allmain.c`/`spell.c`):\n```c\nint\nenergycost(int spell)\n{\n    int energy;\n\n    energy = 3 * (1 + spell_lev(spell)) / 2;  /* level 1: 3, level 2: 4, ... */\n    if (spell_lev(spell) > 1) energy *= (1 + ...);\n    ...\n}\n```\nHmm, but actually I recall in 3.6:\n```c\n/* energycost: return the energy cost of casting spell */\nint\nenergycost(int spell)\n{\n    int energy;\n\n    energy = 3 + 2 * (spell_lev(spell) - 1);  /* spells cost 3 energy per level */\n    ...\n}\n```\nStill 3 for level 1.\n\nHmm — but wait! Maybe the issue is that `blstats.energy` is being read when it's 6, and 193 failures happen. The wizard's energy regen: +1 every 2 turns roughly. Casting force bolt costs 3. So 193 attempts failing is a lot. But the run only had... let me check turns. The output was truncated; I only saw the tail. The run finished in 3.3 seconds — that's very short! The baseline seed 0 run took ~20-30s and 13697 turns. 3.3 seconds means the episode ended almost immediately.\n\nLet me look at the top of the output to see turns, death, err. The tail cut it off. That's the key — the episode probably crashed/ended early.\n\nActually \"err\" wasn't shown in the tail. Let me re-check the JSON.\n\nThe 3.3s runtime strongly suggests the episode terminated early (e.g., death or an error). Let me read the JSON head.","time":{"start":1790680865817,"end":1790680869622}}}
