{"type":"reasoning","timestamp":1790680882429,"sessionID":"ses_f132db44effejOC7YW0uFAg7SL","part":{"id":"prt_0ece5c122001XKYtA1wlo2gCBF","messageID":"msg_0ece5bcd1001yMp2jbcIyW9TOf","sessionID":"ses_f132db44effejOC7YW0uFAg7SL","type":"reasoning","text":"The real problem: infinite loop. The agent keeps trying to cast with insufficient energy, in a tight loop, generating no turns, and hits the 200-step inactivity counter.\n\nWhy does `can_cast` say yes? Because `blstats.energy` >= 3 but the game says no energy. Hmm, OR: `blstats.energy` isn't decreasing and the wizard's energy is 0, and my cost estimate is wrong.\n\nWait — actually. Hmm! Let me reconsider: maybe `best_attack_spell()` returns 'force bolt' but... Let me check `spell_levels`. `parse_spellcast_view` sets `spell_levels['force bolt'] = 1`. `spell_energy_cost` = 3. So can_cast requires energy >= 3.\n\nHmm, so with energy 0 it should return None. Unless... `get_priorities`/`get_available_actions` is being evaluated when energy is high, and then during the *fight2* loop, the priority list is recomputed each iteration? Let me check: `get_priorities` is called in `fight2`? Let me look at how the action list is refreshed.\n\nActually the crucial question: is the list recomputed each turn inside fight2? If it's computed once and reused for many turns, then a cast action stays in the list even after energy is spent. Then `_fight2_perform_action` gets ('cast',...) with no energy → repeated \"You don't have enough energy\" and a stall.\n\nBut 193 failures over 848 turns means it was recomputed many times. And it never raised on the `assert self.character.can_cast(spell_name)` — because energy stayed >= 3.\n\nSo energy really is >= 3 but the game refuses. Therefore the energy cost of force bolt is > 3... but energy was 6 at the start. Hmm, unless energy is NOT 6.\n\nWait, hold on! Maybe the wizard is not the one casting — could `blstats.energy` reflect the *kitten*? No.\n\nLet me just empirically measure: print energy and try casting. Let me write a tiny focused probe: read the book, then repeatedly try `agent.cast('force bolt', dir)` printing energy before/after and the message.\n\nActually — WAIT. I bet I know. NetHack's message for insufficient energy in 3.6 is:\n```c\nif (u.uen < energycost(spell)) {\n    pline(\"You don't have enough energy to cast that spell.\");\n    ...\n}\n```\nAnd `energycost` in NetHack 3.6:\n```c\nint\nenergycost(int spell)\n{\n    int energy;\n\n    energy = 3 + 2 * (spell_lev(spell) - 1);\n    energy *= (1 + SpellBook_traditional_cost_bonus);   /* = 1 for basic magic */\n    ...\n}\n```\nSo force bolt = 3.\n\nUnless... the wizard is *impaired*! \"You are too impaired\" is a different message. Hmm.\n\nOR: **The spell is not actually force bolt.** `known_spells` from the *first* parse may include other spells learned later. But `best_attack_spell` picks min fail. At the start only force bolt (0% fail) and haste self (91%). If a *better* attack spell with 0% fail appears... no.\n\nHmm, let me look again at the actual message sequence: \"You don't have enough energy to cast that spell. Unknown command ' '.\" — 193 times, and no \"Choose which spell\" complaints.\n\nLet me just measure directly. Quick probe.","time":{"start":1790680875298,"end":1790680882424}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1790680886807,"sessionID":"ses_f132db44effejOC7YW0uFAg7SL","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"write","callID":"call_function_snogpsu1kffi_1","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"\"\"\"Measure the energy cost of force bolt directly.\"\"\"\nimport contextlib, os, sys, tempfile, threading, time, warnings\nfrom pathlib import Path\ncache = Path(tempfile.gettempdir()) / \"nethack_arena_submission_cache\"\ncache.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\nos.environ.setdefault(\"XDG_CACHE_HOME\", str(cache / \"xdg\"))\nos.environ.setdefault(\"NUMBA_CACHE_DIR\", str(cache / \"numba\"))\nwarnings.filterwarnings(\"ignore\", category=RuntimeWarning)\nsys.path.insert(0, \"/workspace\")\nfrom nethackers.arena.environment import NLEEnvironment\nfrom nethackers.arena.seeds import trajectory_spec\nfrom nle.nethack import ACTIONS as _ACTIONS\nimport nle.nethack as nh\nfrom nle.nethack import actions as Ac\nfrom autoascend import agent as A\n\n\nclass DirectEnv:\n    def __init__(self, env):\n        self.env, self.agent, self.t0, self.budget = env, None, time.time(), 1e18\n\n    def step(self, action):\n        res = self.env.step(_ACTIONS.index(action))\n        if time.time() - self.t0 > self.budget:\n            raise RuntimeError(\"budget\")\n        return res[0], res[1], res[2], {}\n\n    def debug_tiles(self, *a, **k):\n        return contextlib.nullcontext()\n\n    def debug_log(self, *a, **k):\n        return contextlib.nullcontext()\n\n\ndef run():\n    env = NLEEnvironment(1_000_000, 10_000, \"wiz-hum-cha-mal\")\n    env.reset(trajectory_spec(\"public\", \"local\", 0))\n    d = DirectEnv(env)\n    ag = A.Agent(d, panic_on_errors=False)\n    d.agent = ag\n    with ag.atom_operation():\n        ag.step(Ac.Command.ESC)\n        ag.step(Ac.Command.ESC)\n        ag.character.parse()\n    book = [i for i in ag.inventory.items if i.category == nh.SPBOOK_CLASS][0]\n    with ag.atom_operation():\n        ag.step(Ac.Command.READ)\n        ag.type_text(ag.inventory.items.get_letter(book))\n        for _ in range(4):\n            if 'memorize' in ag.message:\n                break\n            if 'Continue?' in ag.message:\n                ag.type_text('y')\n            else:\n                ag.type_text(' ')\n    print(\"read ->\", repr(ag.message))\n    ag.character.parse_spellcast_view()\n    print(\"known\", ag.character.known_spells, \"levels\", ag.character.spell_levels,\n          \"fail\", ag.character.spell_fail_chance)\n    print(\"cost\", ag.character.spell_energy_cost('force bolt'))\n    for t in range(30):\n        ag.direction('.')\n        if not ag.character.prop.blind:\n            break\n    print(\"energy\", ag.blstats.energy, \"max\", ag.blstats.energy_max, \"turn\", ag.blstats.time)\n    for i in range(6):\n        e0 = ag.blstats.energy\n        with ag.atom_operation():\n            ag.step(Ac.Command.CAST)\n            ag.type_text(ag.character.known_spells['force bolt'])\n            for _ in range(3):\n                if 'In what direction?' in ag.message:\n                    break\n                ag.type_text(' ')\n            ok = 'In what direction?' in ag.message\n            if ok:\n                ag.step(Ac.CompassDirection.E)\n        print(f\"  try {i}: ene {e0}->{ag.blstats.energy} asked={ok} msg={ag.message!r}\")\n        for _ in range(12):\n            ag.direction('.')\n    env.close()\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    sys.setrecursionlimit(100000)\n    threading.stack_size(256 * 1024 * 1024)\n    t = threading.Thread(target=run)\n    t.start()\n    t.join()\n","filePath":"/home/agent/nhwork/probe4.py"},"output":"Wrote file successfully.","metadata":{"diagnostics":{},"filepath":"/home/agent/nhwork/probe4.py","exists":false,"truncated":false},"title":"home/agent/nhwork/probe4.py","time":{"start":1790680886797,"end":1790680886804}},"id":"prt_0ece5dcfa001pBiZrkc2ntkscu","sessionID":"ses_f132db44effejOC7YW0uFAg7SL","messageID":"msg_0ece5bcd1001yMp2jbcIyW9TOf"}}
