{"type":"reasoning","timestamp":1790680935291,"sessionID":"ses_f132db44effejOC7YW0uFAg7SL","part":{"id":"prt_0ece69c4b001cRANvNAk7312FV","messageID":"msg_0ece696cf001JNlt4mjpJq2vLh","sessionID":"ses_f132db44effejOC7YW0uFAg7SL","type":"reasoning","text":"So melee priority is typically 16 (1 + 15), and ranged is 11 (or 0 when a monster is adjacent, which deprioritizes throwing at an adjacent monster). And the max is taken. So melee (16) beats ranged (11) normally. And my cast priority of 20 beats melee. Good — 20 > 16, so casting is preferred over melee.\n\nHmm, but is casting at point-blank range a good idea? Force bolt at range 1 works (it's a ray). Forcing the wizard to always cast instead of melee could be bad when adjacent to a dangerous monster, since casting costs energy and if it fails you're hit anyway. But force bolt with 0% fail and 3.5 avg damage (1d6+1, 1-3 bolts) is better than an unskilled quarterstaff (1d6+0, no to-hit bonus... actually an unskilled quarterstaff does 1d6). Hmm, force bolt 1-3 bolts × (1d6+1) is much stronger. Plus it hits at range.\n\nBut safety: if the monster is adjacent, being at range doesn't help. Still, the spell is better damage. Let me keep cast at 20 but reduce it when a monster is adjacent, so melee gets a chance... Actually no — simpler is better. Let me first fix the stall and measure.\n\nLet me now add the cooldown guard.\n\nAlso, I realize I should double check: is `melee` 16 always? `ret = 1; if hitpoints > 8 or is_monster_faster: ret += 15`. So if HP <= 8 and the monster is not faster, melee is 1 → very low. So at low HP the bot would still cast (20). Hmm, that's when you want to NOT waste energy. But casting at low HP is exactly when you want the ranged attack. It's fine.\n\nLet me now implement the cooldown.","time":{"start":1790680931403,"end":1790680935287}}}
