{"type":"reasoning","timestamp":1790680990701,"sessionID":"ses_f132db44effejOC7YW0uFAg7SL","part":{"id":"prt_0ece7681b001WCCzg2KH9qKH1E","messageID":"msg_0ece763b4001JXpX5eQgsSo4hi","sessionID":"ses_f132db44effejOC7YW0uFAg7SL","type":"reasoning","text":"The XP rate is dramatically better:\n- baseline: xp2 at 316, xp3 at 1234, xp4 at 2943, xp5 at 5567, xp6 at 7812\n- new: xp2 at 994, xp3 at 1679, xp4 at 2700, xp5 at 4135\n\nHmm, xp2 is SLOWER (994 vs 316) but everything after is much faster: xp3 1679 vs 1234, xp4 2700 vs 2943, xp5 4135 vs 5567. So by turn 4135 the new version is at xp5 vs baseline's xp5 at 5567. That's a ~35% speedup in XP.\n\nWait, but baseline hit xp6 at 7812 and the new one only hit xp5 at 4135 and then lost the level at 7900. The new run died at 8052 due to starvation.\n\nSo: the change clearly accelerates XP, but the run died early from starvation (fainting repeatedly). In the baseline, at 12834 it lost xp6→5 then regained at 12851.\n\nThe key difference: the new run survived only 8052 turns and starved. So the death is the bottleneck, not XP.\n\nNote \"faint from lack of food\" appears 9 times in the new run. Let me check the baseline's message histogram for fainting. Let me compare.\n\nAlso: the baseline's xp2 at 316 vs new 994 — because in the new run the wizard reads the spellbook early (turn ~40), which costs turns, and it takes a while before the first kill.\n\nActually more likely: the early game is the same, and the divergence starts later. Baseline xp2 at 316 (turn 316, ~40 kills?), new xp2 at 994. Hmm, that's a big early difference. Let me look at the new run's early phase... Actually it doesn't matter much: the metric is the *final* max XP level reached before the episode ends. Getting to xp5 by turn 4135 vs 5567 is a real win, but the run then died at 8052 instead of surviving to 13697.\n\nThe right move now: run the full 15-seed evaluation to get the real paired comparison. 4 minutes. Let me do that.\n\nBut first let me double check there's no crash risk: n_panics 20 on this seed. Panics are handled (panic_on_errors in the arena?). Let me make sure the arena adapter sets panic_on_errors=False or handles them. The baseline had 122 panics, so panics are tolerated.\n\nLet me run the full arena evaluation now.\n\nAlso, I should double check `read_spellbook` for a potential issue: the `atom_operation` with the loop of 5 type_text calls. If a monster attacks during that, fine.\n\nOne more concern: `learn_spells` yields False if `self.character.known_spells` is non-empty. After learning force bolt, `known_spells` is non-empty forever → never reads another book. That means it never learns better spells. That's intentional for a \"focused change\" but limits upside. Since ATTACK_SPELL_DAMAGE only covers a few spells, and force bolt is 0% fail, it's a solid baseline. Keep it simple.\n\nLet me now run the 15-seed paired eval.","time":{"start":1790680983580,"end":1790680990697}}}
