{"type":"reasoning","timestamp":1790681308473,"sessionID":"ses_f132db44effejOC7YW0uFAg7SL","part":{"id":"prt_0ecec3ad5001TB5RK8GnSJykfC","messageID":"msg_0ecec336b00161963UbKwy6Kon","sessionID":"ses_f132db44effejOC7YW0uFAg7SL","type":"reasoning","text":"Mixed: mean 0.0554 vs baseline 0.0624 — slightly worse, 5 forward / 6 backward.\n\nThe big wins are on seeds 0, 3, 10 (early-death seeds: +0.0376, +0.0537, +0.0504). The big losses are on seeds 4, 7, 11, 14 (-0.15, -0.0376, -0.0425, -0.0454).\n\nInteresting pattern: the *backward* seeds all die much EARLIER (6863 vs 32346, 5217 vs 11919, 12817 vs 23971, 7833 vs 22485, 20371 vs 27094). So the change is making some runs die earlier. The wins are on runs that previously died early and now survive long.\n\nSo: casting helps survival on some seeds but hurts on others. Why would casting hurt? Possible reasons:\n\n1. **Energy starvation**: casting drains energy, and energy regenerates while resting. The wizard now spends turns casting instead of eating/resting → hunger. Seed 5 died of starvation. Seed 6 ended with cause None at 5217 turns (step limit? no, 15000 steps). Hmm, \"None\" cause with 5217 turns — probably an error. Let me check seed 6's status/error!\n\nThat's important: `end_status` and `error` for seeds 6 and 8 (8 also has cause None). Let me check for errors — an error would zero or truncate the episode.\n\n2. **Priority 20 is too aggressive**: casting at every opportunity, even when the spell fizzles or when a monster is adjacent and the wizard would rather swing. Also force bolt costs energy that the wizard needs.\n\n3. Casting makes the wizard *not* melee, and force bolt (1-3 bolts of 1d6+1) vs a quarterstaff... but the unarmed quarterstaff is \"unskilled\", so force bolt should be better. Except: force bolt's damage is 1d6+1 per bolt with 1-3 bolts — average ~1-2 bolts... Actually the \"N bolts\" in NetHack force bolt is based on caster level: 1 bolt for level 1-2, 2 for 3-5, 3 for 6+. So 1 bolt at level 1: 1d6+1 ≈ 4.5 damage. The unskilled quarterstaff: 1d6 = 3.5 + 0 str bonus. So similar, but force bolt doesn't depend on to-hit (it always hits) and doesn't cost a turn of... hmm, both cost a turn.\n\nHmm, so at level 1-2 the spell is a modest damage upgrade with perfect accuracy. That shouldn't be *worse*.\n\n4. **The real problem may be the energy economy.** Casting 3 energy per bolt. The wizard's max energy at XP1 is 6, XP2 = 20, XP3 = 30... Energy regen is +1 per 2 turns (or faster when resting). If the wizard casts every turn it has energy, it's spending turns that could be spent eating/searching, and — importantly — **the wizard must be well-fed**.\n\n5. Or: **casting reveals position / attracts attention**? Not really.\n\n6. Or the `read_spellbook` at the start costs turns & causes blindness at a bad time.\n\nLet me look at the biggest loss, seed 4: 6863 turns vs 32346, died to a gecko at Xp:5 vs Xp:10. That's a huge regression. Something systematic.\n\nLet me diagnose seeds 4 and 14 with the diag script to see what's happening. And check errors for seeds 6 and 8.\n\nLet me first check the `error` field for all seeds in cand1.","time":{"start":1790681299669,"end":1790681308465}}}
