ocal\" baseline run! The published baseline numbers match the \"local\" run. I should re-run the candidate with `--evaluation-id local` to make the comparison valid.\n\nThat would explain the weirdness: seeds 4, 7, 11, 14 losing badly.\n\nLet me verify by re-running the candidate with evaluation-id local. That's the correct paired comparison.\n\nActually, let me double check first: does `evaluation_id` affect public seeds? Let me look at trajectory_spec.\n\nAlso seed 4's diag run also diverged from the arena (24395 vs 6863). The diag uses \"local\". The baseline arena also used \"local\" and matched. So the candidate-with-\"cand1\" run is the odd one out → different seeds. Confirmed hypothesis.\n\nLet me re-run the evaluation with `--evaluation-id local`.","time":{"start":1790681415314,"end":1790681421437}}}
