{"type":"reasoning","timestamp":1790682141450,"sessionID":"ses_f132db44effejOC7YW0uFAg7SL","part":{"id":"prt_0ecf8f941001If6AgYozOyqA41","messageID":"msg_0ecf8f4b4001GoHVKslBqBOT5f","sessionID":"ses_f132db44effejOC7YW0uFAg7SL","type":"reasoning","text":"So zapping exists and is a full path-simulation feature. `is_offensive_usable_wand()` — does magic missile qualify? And the priority is `min(p,1)*10 - 15` = -5 for a weak monster (10-15), or `p*25 - 15`. Ranged (dagger throw) is 11, melee 16. So zapping a weak monster scores -5, way below ranged 11 and melee 16 → never used against weak monsters. Against a dangerous monster, p*25-15 could be 10 → still below 11. So the wand is essentially never used.\n\nSo the wand of magic missile (8 charges, free damage) is unused because its priority formula is too low. Interesting — but \"fix the wand priority\" is a tuning change that could be seed-agnostic and beneficial.\n\nHmm, but careful: I have limited compute. The 45-seed A/B is running. Let me think about which single change has the best mechanism.\n\nLet me reconsider. Actually, let me reconsider the whole framing. The evaluation is dominated by *when the wizard dies*, which is chaotic. With 45 seeds I'll get a standard error of maybe 0.008 on the mean. Differences of ~0.008 are detectable-ish.\n\nLet me now think about what the *strongest* systematic lever is, given everything I know:\n\nThe wizard is fragile: 12 HP at start, AC ~8-10 (no armor? it has a cloak of magic resistance and a ring). It dies to a jackal, a bat, a newt, a giant rat, a fox, a hobbit. These are all *weak* monsters that a 1d6+1 staff shouldn't lose to... unless the bot fights them badly or gets surrounded, or its HP is low from starvation.\n\n**Starvation** is the recurring systemic issue: I saw \"You faint from lack of food\" 17 times on seed 0, and multiple seeds dying of starvation/gas-spore-while-fainting. A fainting wizard at 3 HP is dead meat. The wizard is level 1-2 for the first 1000 turns, and low-level wizards have tiny stomachs (a wiz's max hunger is small and they burn through it).\n\nThe bot has `eat_corpes_from_ground` and food strategies, but maybe it isn't prioritizing food. In the very first turn analysis, the messages showed \"There is a lichen corpse here; eat it? [ynq] (n)\" and \"This lichen corpse tastes okay.\" So it does eat.\n\nHmm, is this \"starvation\" actually a *baseline* problem too? Let me check the baseline causes of death. Let me look at baseline.json.\n\nLet me do that now while waiting.","time":{"start":1790682134849,"end":1790682141426}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1790682142068,"sessionID":"ses_f132db44effejOC7YW0uFAg7SL","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"call_function_uviajga90nom_1","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /home/agent/nhwork && python -c \"\nimport json\nb=json.load(open('baseline.json'))\nfor r in sorted(b,key=lambda r:r['trajectory_id']):\n    print(r['trajectory_id'], r['turns'], r['milestone'], r['max_depth'], '|', r['cause_of_death'])\n\""},"output":"0 13697 Xp:6 1 | killed by a goblin\n1 17693 Xp:6 1 | killed by a jackal\n2 20700 Xp:8 5 | killed by a white unicorn\n3 3052 Xp:3 1 | killed by a grid bug\n4 32346 Xp:10 7 | killed by a wolf\n5 14486 Xp:7 1 | killed by a bat\n6 11919 Xp:6 1 | killed by a kitten\n7 23971 Xp:8 2 | killed by a rothe\n8 23604 Xp:8 5 | killed by a soldier ant\n9 24295 Xp:8 4 | killed by an ape\n10 4014 Xp:4 1 | killed by a hobbit\n11 27094 Xp:9 5 | killed by a wolf\n12 12509 Xp:6 1 | killed by a newt\n13 5206 Xp:4 1 | died of starvation\n14 22485 Xp:8 1 | killed by a crossbow bolt\n","metadata":{"output":"0 13697 Xp:6 1 | killed by a goblin\n1 17693 Xp:6 1 | killed by a jackal\n2 20700 Xp:8 5 | killed by a white unicorn\n3 3052 Xp:3 1 | killed by a grid bug\n4 32346 Xp:10 7 | killed by a wolf\n5 14486 Xp:7 1 | killed by a bat\n6 11919 Xp:6 1 | killed by a kitten\n7 23971 Xp:8 2 | killed by a rothe\n8 23604 Xp:8 5 | killed by a soldier ant\n9 24295 Xp:8 4 | killed by an ape\n10 4014 Xp:4 1 | killed by a hobbit\n11 27094 Xp:9 5 | killed by a wolf\n12 12509 Xp:6 1 | killed by a newt\n13 5206 Xp:4 1 | died of starvation\n14 22485 Xp:8 1 | killed by a crossbow bolt\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"cd /home/agent/nhwork && python -c \"\nimport json\nb=json.load(open('baseline.json'))\nfor r in sorted(b,key=lambda r:r['trajectory_id']):\n    print(r['trajectory_id'], r['turns'], r['milestone'], r['max_depth'], '|', r['cause_of_death'])\n\"","time":{"start":1790682141744,"end":1790682141970}},"id":"prt_0ecf91302001tdg2Cx09ij