{"type":"reasoning","timestamp":1790683583227,"sessionID":"ses_f132db44effejOC7YW0uFAg7SL","part":{"id":"prt_0ed0f0c18001XzV0V0qCN48R9I","messageID":"msg_0ed0f00d7001pe7txElZljthSP","sessionID":"ses_f132db44effejOC7YW0uFAg7SL","type":"reasoning","text":"**AC stays at 9 for 13,000 turns.** The wizard is naked the whole game. AC 9 means most monsters hit 80% of the time.\n\nIf the wizard picked up and wore a robe/armor (AC 6-8) or used a shield, its AC could drop to 5-7. That's a *massive* systematic survival improvement — the single highest-leverage change available.\n\nAnd it fits: the wizard has 12-34 gold and never buys anything. Gold 12 at turn 4000. It's not shopping!\n\nDoes the bot have any shopping/armor logic? Let me check for armor equipping. `autoascend/item/inventory.py` has item categories. Let me grep for ARMOR / equip.\n\nThis is a much stronger lever than casting. Let me investigate.","time":{"start":1790683581464,"end":1790683583223}}}
