{"type":"reasoning","timestamp":1790683660713,"sessionID":"ses_f132db44effejOC7YW0uFAg7SL","part":{"id":"prt_0ed10043c0014qb7d2jjRunX69","messageID":"msg_0ed0fd1ef001OZEfemerfU0tpq","sessionID":"ses_f132db44effejOC7YW0uFAg7SL","type":"reasoning","text":"Very informative:\n1. The wizard wears a **+0 iron skull cap** from turn 4009 (AC 9 → 8). That's the only armor in 13697 turns. Armor is rare on dlvl 1-5, so this is a supply problem, not a behavior problem. Armor is not worth a focused change.\n\n2. **A wand of magic missile (0:8) is in the pack from turn 403 and is never used** — the charges go 8 → 7 → 6 → 4 → 3, so it IS being fired occasionally (autopickup/explore fires it? no — those are the *same wand* with decreasing charges... interesting, it goes 8, 7, 6, 4, 3). So the wand is used sometimes. Hmm, actually those are all the same wand being zapped. So the wand IS being used (5 charges over 13000 turns).\n\nWait, no. Let me re-read: at t=403 there's \"a wand of magic missile (0:8)\". At 4009 \"(0:7)\", at 6020 \"(0:6)\", at 7625 \"(0:4)\", at 8027 \"(0:3)\". So 5 charges were used between turn 4009 and 8027. Hmm, and the printed list only shows *new distinct* text values, so I'm seeing the charge-count variants. So yes, the wand is being zapped occasionally.\n\n3. **The inventory is full of junk**: 2 crude daggers, 3 crude daggers, 4 crude daggers, 5 crude daggers, 6 crude daggers, 9 darts, corroded daggers... The wizard is picking up dozens of daggers/darts and carrying them! This could cause \"You are carrying too much junk\" → the wizard must drop items (wasting turns), or the weight slows it down. Actually more importantly: carrying lots of junk means *dropping* junk to pick up better loot, wasting turns.\n\n4. There's an enchant armor scroll ×2 (one blessed!) never used. And a scroll of gold detection, and a \"READ ME\" scroll (the famous advice scroll, which would tell the bot how to play!). And a scroll labeled GHOTI (summons a horde!) and TEMOV.\n\nSo there are several unexploited items, but \"use the enchant armor scroll\" is a weak change.\n\nLet me step back and think about the biggest lever again with this new information:\n\n**The wizard's HP is tiny (12-46) and it has AC 8-9. It dies to everything.** The single most effective survival lever for a low-level wizard: **more HP**. The ring of gain constitution (+1 CON) is in the pack at t=403 and is *never equipped* (eq=False)! Equipping a blessed +1 CON ring gives +2-3 max HP (CON 3 → 4 = +1 HP per level... small).\n\nHmm. Small.\n\n**The real observation: the bot is carrying 6+ crude daggers and 9 darts.** Why? Because it picks up anything and drops nothing. In NetHack, carrying excess junk has a real cost: it fills inventory letters, and dropping requires turns. But more importantly, weight doesn't slow you in NetHack.\n\nOK so let me think about what actually kills it and what would systematically help.\n\nLet me reconsider: the wizard has an **unskilled quarterstaff** and throws **darts** (it has 9 darts, and at_ready). Darts are ranged attacks that mostly work. The baseline throws 195 darts on seed 0.\n\nHmm, what about **training the quarterstaff**? A \"focused change\" to spend turns practicing the quarterstaff would make melee much stronger (to-hit and damage). A level-1 wizard practicing a quarterstaff for 200 turns gets +2 to-hit/+2 damage. That's a real, systematic combat improvement... but it costs turns.\n\nOK, let me take yet another step back and think about the *meta* structure of this benchmark task. The instruction is to make one focused change that raises the score. Given the measurement noise (SE ~0.005-0.008 on 45 seeds), I need a change worth >0.015 mean, i.e. it must move many seeds by a full milestone.\n\nLet me reconsider the data ONE more time, looking for the biggest systematic deficit:\n\nBaseline 45 seeds: 13 at Xp:8, 6 at Xp:7, 9 at Xp:6, 3 at Xp:5, 3 at Xp:4, 3 at Xp:3, 2 at Xp:2, 2 at Xp:10, 2 at Xp:9, 1 Dlvl:5, 2 None.\n\nSo 28/45 seeds are at Xp:6-Xp:8 — the \"stalled\" group. The wizard gets to XP 6-8 and then stops gaining XP. Why?! It has ~15000-25000 turns. It should keep killing.\n\nLet me look at the kill rate over time on seed 0: 190 kills in 13697 turns. If it kills at that rate, by 25000 turns it would have ~350 kills. The XP needed for XP 6→7 is 250, 7→8 is 300, 8→9 is 500. Each kill gives XP based on the monster's difficulty. So reaching XP 8 takes ~40-50 kills, and XP 9 takes another ~60-80 kills. So the XP curve flattens naturally.\n\nHmm, so the wizard is XP-limited by kill count, and kill count is limited by turns. The bot spends most turns NOT killing. 190 kills in 13697 turns = 1 kill per 72 turns. That's the inefficiency. Where do 72 turns per kill go? Searching (1382), exploring/walking, resting, eating, dealing with items.\n\n**If I could double the kill rate, the wizard would reach XP 10-12 instead of 6-8, and the score would jump a lot.** Xp:10 = 0.179, Xp:12 = ~0.24+.\n\nSo kill rate IS the lever, and the spell gave +26% XP rate but at the cost of dying sooner. Hmm, but why did it die sooner?\n\nLet me re-examine: in cand2, mean turns went 15114 → 14578 (slightly worse) while the mean score went +0.0011. So the spell neither improved nor hurt.\n\nLet me reconsider the *biggest* structural inefficiency: 1382 SEARCH actions (9% of all steps) on dlvl 1-2 where traps are rare. And the `# terrain` command 169 times. And 'EXTCMD' 169 times, 'LOOK' 14...\n\nLet me quantify from the seed 0 action histogram (baseline): SEARCH 1382, NUM_5 997 (darts thrown), SPACE 586, E 530, W 529, SW 353, S 325, N 285, NW 271, SE 218, ESC 216, EAT 201, NE 198, THROW 195, MORE 178, EXTCMD 169, LOOK 157, MOVEFAR 157, APPLY 116.\n\nTotal steps 15013. SEARCH = 1382 (9.2%). Movement ~2800 (19%). NUM_5 = throw dart 997 (6.6%).\n\nHmm, so where does the other ~65% of steps go? The histogram I have only showed the top ~20. Let me get the full baseline action histogram. Let me re-run the diag and dump all actions.\n\nThat will show me where the turns actually go. This is the right way to find the lever. Let me do it.","time":{"start":1790683644988,"end":1790683660708}}}
