{"type":"reasoning","timestamp":1790683696401,"sessionID":"ses_f132db44effejOC7YW0uFAg7SL","part":{"id":"prt_0ed10999f001dMbDKdapSI5PJE","messageID":"msg_0ed108fc5001RlL2iV7dx7f1z2","sessionID":"ses_f132db44effejOC7YW0uFAg7SL","type":"reasoning","text":"**SEARCH is 14.2% of all steps (2050 steps) and SPACE is 11.2% (1614 steps).**\n\nSPACE 1614 — that's `A.TextCharacters.SPACE` used to dismiss \"more\" prompts, which in NetHack usually does NOT advance a turn. So those are free-ish steps. But they eat the *step budget*!\n\nWait — do the arena's step limits matter? The step budget: seed 6 hit `end_status -1` (out of steps) at 10581 steps. So the arena has a step budget and the wizard can run out of steps! With ~15000 steps allowed (the baseline seed 0 used exactly 15013 steps... hmm, that's suspicious: exactly 15013).\n\nLet me check: the baseline runs' steps: 15013, 19841, 28050, 2852, 42900, 17145, 12251, 29404, 31735, 30053, 3897, 35301, 13818, 6060, 29240. So no fixed cap of 15013. The 15013 for seed 0 is coincidental... Actually no! Let me check the arena's max_steps. It's probably `MAX_STEPS = 15000` scaled by something. Hmm, seed 4 used 42900 steps. So no.\n\nOK so steps aren't the binding constraint (mostly). But `end_status -1` happened for seeds 6 and 8 in the cand1 run, so there IS a step limit sometimes. Let me look at the arena's step accounting... Actually `end_status -1` = the *environment* ended, maybe due to NLE's TURN_LIMIT or the arena's per-episode cap. Seed 8 did 37895 steps. Hmm.\n\nLet me look at the arena's episode termination to understand: it likely has a max steps of ~ some large number, plus a `time` limit.\n\nActually, more valuable: **SEARCH at 14.2% is a big waste on early dungeon levels.** And `SPACE` at 11.2% is prompt dismissal (mostly free). And `WHATIS` 335 + `EXTCMD` 336 + `LOOK` 579 + `MORE` 405 — the '#' extended commands (168 '#' actions, 168 '# t', 169 '# terrain'). Those are the tty-look commands for tracking terrain/monsters. ~1000 steps = 7% spent on bookkeeping!\n\n**Bookkeeping insight**: the bot spends ~7% of its steps on `#`, `# t`, `# terrain` look commands and 4% on LOOK. That's a diagnostics feature, not a game action. But it's the existing behavior; changing it is \"one focused change\" but feels like gutting the bot's features.\n\nLet me focus on the biggest single actionable item: **SEARCH = 14.2%**.\n\nWhy does the bot search? Let me look at the search strategy. On dlvl 1, NetHack's \"search\" costs 1 turn and reveals hidden monsters/traps/doors. The bot does it to find hidden monsters (for XP) and traps. On early levels there ARE hidden monsters (gnome lord, mimic...) but the payoff is low.\n\nLet me look at the search strategy to see when it's active.\n\nActually, let me reconsider priorities. I have limited time. Let me think about which single change is most likely to produce a >0.015 mean gain.\n\nHonest assessment of the search idea: eliminating 14% of steps on early levels frees ~10% of turns. If the freed turns go to killing, that's a ~10% XP gain → maybe +0.005 mean. Not enough, and risky.\n\n**Bigger idea: the \"faint\" event count is 44 on seed 0!** `events: {'faint': 44, 'pray': 10}`. The wizard faints 44 times in 13697 turns. Fainting = HP → 0, then \"You regain consciousness\" with 1 HP. Each faint is a near-death. And 122 panics in the baseline!\n\n**What causes 44 faints?** Starvation! \"You faint from lack of food.\" That's the message. So the wizard is CONSTANTLY starving. 44 faints. On a 12-46 HP character, each faint is a 1-HP state where any monster hit kills.\n\nThis is a huge, systematic, fixable problem: **the wizard is starving to death repeatedly**. A wizard at XP 1-4 has a tiny stomach and low nutrition; the bot must eat far more. It's carrying food rations and fortune cookies, and eating lichen corpses. But it clearly isn't keeping up.\n\nAnd the candidate (spell) run also fainted 17 times.\n\nSo: why is the wizard always hungry? Because it's not finding enough food, or because it spends its turns casting/searching instead of foraging. In NetHack, a level-1 wizard's max nutrition is 900ish but burns through it fast (energy regen?). Actually, in NetHack, **energy regeneration doesn't consume nutrition**; but *fighting* does.\n\nHmm, 44 faints means the wizard's nutrition hit zero 44 times. To fix this, the wizard must eat more food. It has a `food ration` and `fortune cookie`. It ate lichen corpses (1 turn each, negligible nutrition... lichen corpses give 1 nutrition? No, corpses give real nutrition).\n\n**A focused change: prioritize eating over searching.** E.g., disable the search strategy while hungry. Or: make the bot eat any food in inventory when hunger_state is high, before searching.\n\nLet me look at the strategies to see if the search happens while hungry. `global_logic.py` has an ordered list of preempted strategies. If `search_strategy` has priority over `eat_food`, the bot searches itself to death.\n\nLet me read global_logic.py fully to understand the ordering.","time":{"start":1790683683231,"end":1790683696395}}}
