{"type":"reasoning","timestamp":1790684831793,"sessionID":"ses_f132db44effejOC7YW0uFAg7SL","part":{"id":"prt_0ed220653001zJTurXaN0iUSsA","messageID":"msg_0ed21ffe1001U5UlCsTkaFVwZ3","sessionID":"ses_f132db44effejOC7YW0uFAg7SL","type":"reasoning","text":"While this runs (~26 min), let me review my code changes for quality and make sure the final deliverable is clean.\n\nLet me review all the diffs:\n1. `autoascend/character.py`: ATTACK_SPELL_DAMAGE, known_spells/spell_fail_chance/spell_levels init, parse_spellcast_view rewrite, spell_energy_cost, can_cast, best_attack_spell, plus the `spells_enabled` env check (to be removed) and `import os`.\n2. `autoascend/agent.py`: cast() direction fix + return value, _direction_action, direction() refactor, _read_spellbooks init, read_spellbook, learn_spells (with the hypothesis comment), 'cast' branch in _fight2_perform_action.\n3. `autoascend/combat/fight_heur.py`: cast_priority, cast action block, 'cast' in the no-combat-action check, Character import.\n4. `autoascend/global_logic.py`: learn_spells preempt.\n5. `autoascend/stats_logger.py`: read_spellbook/learned_spell counters.\n6. `autoascend/combat/utils.py`: 'cast' action_str.\n\nLet me review the hypothesis comment and make sure it's accurate and well-placed. Let me re-read it.\n\nAlso: I should double-check the `learn_spells` placement in the strategy chain. It's preempted after `cure_disease` and before eating. Hmm — that means the wizard reads a spellbook BEFORE eating. Reading blinds it, which is a bit risky if hungry. Better to put it after the eat strategies so hunger comes first. Actually, it only triggers at the very start (once known_spells is non-empty it never runs again), and at the start the wizard isn't hungry. But logically eating should take precedence. Let me move it after the eat block for safety.\n\nHmm, but careful: moving it changes behavior (the spellbook would be read after eating). At game start there's nothing to eat, so it makes no difference in practice. But for robustness, eating should come first. Let me move it to just after the eat preempt block and before `follow_guard`.\n\nLet me also reconsider: `read_spellbook` uses `self.atom_operation()` and types up to 5 times. If the wizard is hit while blind... acceptable.\n\nOne issue: `learn_spells` yields False if `self.character.known_spells` is non-empty — but `known_spells` is only populated by `parse_spellcast_view`, which is called in `read_spellbook`. If the wizard learns a spell, it never reads another book. That's intentional (focused change) but means the wand/book of haste self is ignored. Fine.\n\nAnother consideration: the `AUTOASCEND_SPELLS` env var must be removed before delivery. Let me note that.\n\nLet me now re-read the current state of my edits to make sure everything is clean and correct. Let me view the key sections.","time":{"start":1790684825171,"end":1790684831771}}}
