{"type":"reasoning","timestamp":1790684838885,"sessionID":"ses_f132db44effejOC7YW0uFAg7SL","part":{"id":"prt_0ed222fd8001yC5tZSh80198Z4","messageID":"msg_0ed2221c4001g32XC4vicnAr2r","sessionID":"ses_f132db44effejOC7YW0uFAg7SL","type":"reasoning","text":"The code looks good. Let me improve the hypothesis comment to reflect the final design (range ≥ 2, the measured 5-energy cost) and move `learn_spells` after the eat strategies.\n\nLet me also reconsider the comment's claim \"it casts nothing and zaps nothing\" — the wand was zapped 5 times over the run (charges 8→3). So \"zaps nothing\" is not exactly right. Let me fix that to be accurate: the baseline never casts; the wand is fired a handful of times. Accuracy matters.\n\nLet me rewrite the comment to be accurate and reference the measured facts:\n- score is XP-milestone driven\n- baseline: 190 kills in 13,697 turns on seed 0, all with an unskilled quarterstaff\n- the wizard starts with a blessed spellbook of force bolt (0% fail) and never reads it; 15,013 baseline actions contain no CAST\n- force bolt costs 5 energy and a starting wizard owns 6 total, so it is a ranged weapon, not a melee replacement: at point blank the quarterstaff is strictly better (same damage, no energy)\n- therefore cast only at range >= 2\n- measured: XP5 at turn 4135 vs 5567 (+25% XP rate), panics 122 -> 20\n\nLet me write a tight, accurate version.\n\nThen move learn_spells after the eat block.\n\nLet me do both edits.","time":{"start":1790684835800,"end":1790684838874}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1790684843144,"sessionID":"ses_f132db44effejOC7YW0uFAg7SL","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"edit","callID":"call_function_evzdbfnop99d_1","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/workspace/autoascend/agent.py","newString":"    # hypothesis: this bot is scored on experience level and nothing else -- every\n    # per-seed milestone it ever reaches is an `Xp:N`, every `Dlvl:N` sits below it --\n    # and it is a very slow XP farmer. On seed 0 it takes 13,697 turns and 190 kills to\n    # reach XL 6, swinging an *unskilled* quarterstaff the whole way, while the\n    # character's class mechanic sits unread in its pack: a wiz-hum-cha-mal starts every\n    # game with a blessed spellbook of force bolt (0% fail), and none of the baseline's\n    # 15,013 actions is a cast. Force bolt is not an upgrade to the quarterstaff, though\n    # -- measured in game it costs 5 energy, and a starting wizard's whole pool is 6, so\n    # spending it point blank to deal the same ~1d6 buys nothing. Down a corridor, where\n    # the staff cannot reach at all, it is a free kill that costs no extra time. So:\n    # read the starting spellbook, then cast down a line of sight and keep the staff for\n    # melee. Holding that line took seed 0 to XL 5 on turn 4,135 instead of 5,567 and\n    # cut panics from 122 to 20.\n    def read_spellbook(self, item):","oldString":"    # hypothesis: progression on wiz-hum-cha-mal is decided by experience level and\n    # nothing else -- every published per-seed score is exactly one of the `Xp:N`\n    # milestones and every `Dlvl:N` value is below it -- so this wizard is a pure XP\n    # farmer. It is also a very slow one: 190 kills in 13,697 turns on seed 0, all of\n    # them with an *unskilled* quarterstaff, while the character's whole class mechanic\n    # sits unused in its pack. A wiz-hum-cha-mal starts every game holding a spellbook\n    # of force bolt (0% fail when blessed) and a wand of magic missile, and across