    self.spell_fail_chance = dict()\nautoascend/character.py:368:            self.known_spells[spell_name] = letter\nautoascend/character.py:372:        if self.known_spells:\nautoascend/character.py:388:        if spell_name not in self.known_spells:\nautoascend/character.py:402:        for name, fail in self.spell_fail_chance.items():\nautoascend/agent.py:791:                yield self.character.known_spells[spell_name]\nautoascend/agent.py:842:            self.character.parse_spellcast_view()\nautoascend/agent.py:850:        if self.character.known_spells:\nautoascend/agent.py:1199:                # self.character.parse_spellcast_view()\nautoascend/agent.py:1453:        if 'healing' not in self.character.known_spells:\nautoascend/agent.py:1459:        if self.character.spell_fail_chance['healing'] > 0.2:\nautoascend/agent.py:1466:        if 'extra healing' not in self.character.known_spells:\nautoascend/agent.py:1472:        if self.character.spell_fail_chance['extra healing'] > 0.15:\nautoascend/agent.py:1597:                    # self.character.parse_spellcast_view()\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"cd /workspace && rg -n \"parse_spellcast_view|spell_fail_chance|known_spells\" --glob '*.py' | grep -v \"def \\|self.spell_fail_chance\\[spell_name\\]\\|self.spell_levels\\[spell_name\\]\" | head -20","time":{"start":1790684874076,"end":1790684874168}},"id":"prt_0ed22c3dc001z4QNphEF7G8hHB","sessionID":"ses_f132db44effejOC7YW0uFAg7SL","messageID":"msg_0ed229db2001DpKyQt12Iwz3Av"}}
{"type":"step_finish","timestamp":1790684874266,"sessionID":"ses_f132db44effejOC7YW0uFAg7SL","part":{"id":"prt_0ed22c5c2001bYHpImXMfktM8C","reason":"tool-calls","messageID":"msg_0ed229db2001DpKyQt12Iwz3Av","sessionID":"ses_f132db44effejOC7YW0uFAg7SL","type":"step-finish","tokens":{"total":107544,"input":25,"output":85,"reasoning":731,"cache":{"write":0,"read":106703}},"cost":0}}
{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1790684875996,"sessionID":"ses_f132db44effejOC7YW0uFAg7SL","part":{"id":"prt_0ed22ccc00018YMEMlQBBvory5","messageID":"msg_0ed22c5fe001PCJBV9PeeCUbdC","sessionID":"ses_f132db44effejOC7YW0uFAg7SL","type":"step-start"}}
{"type":"reasoning","timestamp":1790684884775,"sessionID":"ses_f132db44effejOC7YW0uFAg7SL","part":{"id":"prt_0ed22ccd1001vMWW3FYqJsOk18","messageID":"msg_0ed22c5fe001PCJBV9PeeCUbdC","sessionID":"ses_f132db44effejOC7YW0uFAg7SL","type":"reasoning","text":"`parse_spellcast_view` is only called from my new `read_spellbook` (the other two call sites are commented out). So the healer path is unaffected: `should_cast_heal` checks `if 'healing' not in self.character.known_spells: return False` — safe with an empty dict. And since parse_spellcast_view is no longer called at startup (it never was, given the commented-out call sites), the healer behavior is unchanged.\n\nGood. My change to `parse_spellcast_view` (generalizing away the Healer-only guard) is safe: it's only reachable from read_spellbook now, which only runs for Wizards.\n\nHmm, but one thing: my rewrite *removed* the `raise ValueError` for an unexpected popup and replaced it with a soft return. That's a robustness improvement (no panic risk), and it also removed the assertion that caught malformed popups. Acceptable — and safer for a bot that must never crash.\n\nAlso, the old code had a fallback: if there's no popup, `self.known_spells[self.agent.message] = None` (for role-less/monster casting). I dropped that. It was only reachable for Healer, and it's dead code now. Slight behavior change for healers, but since parse_spellcast_view is never called for them, it's inert.\n\nNow let me also double check the `read_spellbook` `'What do you want to read'` condition — I break out of the loop if the message contains \"What do you want to read\", which is the *prompt*. That would break before actually reading! Let me trace: after `self.step(A.Command.READ)`, the game asks \"What do you want to read? [a-z or ?*]\". Then `self.type_text(letter)` sends the letter, and the message becomes \"You begin to memorize the runes.\" So by the time the loop checks, the message should be the result. But if the message still contains the old prompt text (message buffers can be sticky), the loop would break immediately with learned=False.\n\nHmm — that's a bug risk. In the 45-seed runs, learning worked (casts happened), so the message doesn't retain the prompt. But it's fragile. Let me remove that condition — it does nothing useful since we already sent the letter. Actually it was meant to handle \"you have nothing to read\". Let me just drop it to avoid the premature break.\n\nAlso, the loop runs up to 5 iterations, each typing a space. After 'memorize the runes' we break. If the spell is known already (\"You know force bolt quite well already\"), neither branch matches, so we'd type spaces 5 times, producing \"Unknown command\" messages. Minor waste, and it happens only when re-reading the same book (which we avoid via `_read_spellbooks`). Let me add 'already' to the break conditions to be clean. Actually simpler: break on 'memorize' or 'quite well already' or 'unintelligible' or \"don't seem to make sense\".\n\nLet me make those two small robustness fixes.\n\nLet me also reconsider: after reading, the wizard is temporarily blind. `learn_spells` checks for adjacent monsters before reading. Good. But after reading, the wizard is blind and must wait it out — `wait_out_unexpected_state_strategy` handles blindness. Good.\n\nLet me apply the fixes.","time":{"start":1790684875985,"end":1790684884759}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1790684886007,"sessionID":"ses_f132db44effejOC7YW0uFAg7SL","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"edit","callID":"call_function_gixkkloz1c09_1","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/workspace/autoascend/agent.py","newString":"            for _ in range(5):\n                if 'memorize the runes' in self.message or 'unintelligible' in self.message or \\\n                        \"don't seem to make sense\" in self.message or 'quite well already' in self.message:\n                    learned = 'memorize the runes' in self.message\n                    break\n                if 'Continue?' in self.message and not answered_continue:\n                    answered_continue = True\n                    self.type_text('y')\n                    continue\n                self.type_text(' ')","oldString":"            for _ in range(5):\n                if 'memorize the runes' in self.message or 'unintelligible' in self.message or \\\n                        \"don't seem to make sense\" in self.message or 'What do you want to read' in self.message:\n                    learned = 'memorize the runes' in self.message\n                    break\n                if 'Continue?' in self.message and not answered_continue:\n                    answered_continue = True\n                    self.type_text('y')\n                    continue\n                self.type_text(' ')"},"output":"Edit applied successfully.","metadata":{"diagnostics":{},"diff":"Index: /workspace/autoascend/agent.py\n===================================================================\n--- /workspace/autoascend/agent.py\n+++ /workspace/autoascend/agent.py\n@@ -827,9 +827,9 @@\n self.type_text(letter)\n answered_continue = False\n for _ in range(5):\n     if 'memorize the runes' in self.message or 'unintelligible' in self.message or \\\n-            \"don't seem to make sense\" in self.message or 'What do you want to read' in self.message:\n+            \"don't seem to make sense\" in self.message or 'quite well already' in self.message:\n         learned = 'memorize the runes' in self.message\n         break\n     if 'Continue?' in self.message and not answered_continue:\n         answered_continue = True\n","filediff":{"file":"/workspace/autoascend/agent.py","patch":"Index: /workspace/autoascend/agent.py\n===================================================================\n--- /workspace/autoascend/agent.py\n+++ /workspace/autoascend/agent.py\n@@ -827,9 +827,9 @@\n self.type_text(letter)\n answered_continue = False\n for _ in range(5):\n     if 'memorize the runes' in self.message or 'unintelligible' in self.message or \\\n-            \"don't seem to make sense\" in self.message or 'What do you want to read' in self.message:\n+            \"don't seem to make sense\" in self.message or 'quite well already' in self.message:\n         learned = 'memorize the runes' in self.message\n         break\n     if 'Continue?' in self.message and not answered_continue:\n         answered_continue = True\n","additions":1,"deletions":1},"truncated":false},"title":"workspace/autoascend/agent.py","time":{"start":1790684885963,"end":1790684886004}},"id":"prt_0ed22ef20001Y5iaAicBoobSpn","sessionID":"ses_f132db44effejOC7YW0uFAg7SL","messageID":"msg_0ed22c5fe001PCJBV9PeeCUbdC"}}
