{"type":"text","timestamp":1790686960501,"sessionID":"ses_f132db44effejOC7YW0uFAg7SL","part":{"id":"prt_0ed4280f20013ETmdb2wWJQvo4","messageID":"msg_0ed427a65001ql86qqjOX1U9m3","sessionID":"ses_f132db44effejOC7YW0uFAg7SL","type":"text","text":"I reverted the change. Here's where things stand.\n\n## What I tried\n\nA single focused change: **teach the wizard to read its starting spellbook and cast force bolt down a line of sight**, deliberately never displacing the quarterstaff (ranged-only, so melee stays untouched).\n\nMechanics I verified in-game first:\n- Force bolt costs **5 energy** (measured: 6→1), and a starting wizard's whole pool is 6 — so it is a ranged weapon, not a melee upgrade.\n- A blessed spellbook yields 0% fail; the baseline's 15,013 actions contain **zero casts**.\n- NLE exposes no pet-dismiss command (`P` is pray, `CALL` is quaff), so I couldn't test the kitten.\n\n## It worked mechanically, but it did not raise the score\n\n| | result |\n|---|---|\n| XP rate, seed 0 | XL 5 on turn **4,135** vs 5,567 (+25%) |\n| panics, seed 0 | **20** vs 122 |\n| **90 paired seeds (0–89)** | 0.0604 → 0.0574, **−0.0029 ± 0.0054** (t = −0.54, p = 0.59) |\n| forward / backward / same | **39 / 40 / 11** |\n| 15 published seeds | 0.0624 → 0.0574 |\n| mean turns survived | 17,290 → **15,932** (worse) |\n\nAn intermediate 45-seed read looked like +0.0065 (23F/16B). Extending to 90 seeds flipped it to −0.0124 on the new seeds. That was noise, and I'd have shipped a regression on the 45-seed result alone.\n\n## Why no combat tweak can move this\n\nAcross 90 baseline seeds the causes of death are spread almost uniformly over ~60 different monsters (goblin 2, hobbit 4, fox 4, rothe 4, soldier ant 4, jackal 3, wolf 3, kitte 3 — only 6/90 starvation). The wizard dies to whatever lands the killing blow, so the score is a chaotic function of the trajectory. Combined with the milestone structure — moving Xp:7→Xp:8 needs ~136 more kills ≈ 9,800 turns — that sets a hard floor on what's measurable: per-seed SD is 0.033, so the 15-seed mean has SE **0.0085** and even 90 seeds only reaches **0.0054**. Every mechanism I found (casting, early eating, less searching) has an expected effect under 0.01.\n\n## Workspace state\n\nReverted and **verified exact**: all 15 seeds reproduce the published baseline on progress, turns, milestone, and cause of death (0.0624). `arena_adapter.py` untouched; `make_agent`/`reset`/`act` contract intact.\n\n## Should I keep going?\n\nOne idea is left that changes the *plan* rather than the combat, and is the only mechanism I found big enough to clear the noise floor: the bot deliberately farms dlvl 1 until XL 8 at ~1.8 XP per kill, while dlvl 3–5 gives 15–25 XP per kill — and the only seeds that ever scored Xp:9/Xp:10 were the ones sitting at depth 4–5. Descent order is a real 5–10x XP-rate lever rather than a dice re-roll. Testing it on the same 90 seeds costs ~26 minutes of compute.\n\nWant me to run that experiment, or stop here and report the negative result as-is?","time":{"start":1790686953714,"end":1790686960474}}}
